Delorean System Alignment
=========================
Run the script using `python -i <path to delorean_system_alignment> <additional arguments>`
Once the "Press Enter to start laser" prompt is shown the script should drop in to an interactive python environment, which you can verify by seeing '>>>' at beginning of the terminal prompt.

There are 3  commands available here:

Python Commands
===============
stop_laser(db)
steer_rx_to_order(db, order)
steer_tx_to_order(db, order)

Using these commands:
# steer rx to order 5
>>> steer_rx_to_order(db, 5)
# steer tx to order 70
>>> steer_tx_to_order(db, 70)
# stop the laser
>>> stop_laser(db)

In each of these cases the db variable is an instance of the DeloreanBoard class.


Command Line Arguments
======================
    '-z', '--zynq',
    required=True,
    help="Zynq IPv4 address, e.g. '192.168.128.xxx'.")

    '-f', '--freq',
    default=20.,
    type=float,
    help="Pulse repetition frequency in kHz.")

    '-p', '--pw',
    default=5,
    type=int,
    help="Laser drive pulse width index, an int on range(16).")

    '-c', '--ci',
    default=2.5,
    type=float,
    help="iC Haus CI voltage setting in volts, a float <= 5.")

    '-t', '--tx_order',
    default=None,
    type=int,
    help='Order for Tx steering')
    '-r', '--rx_order',
                        default=None,
                        type=int,
                        help='Order for Rx steering')


